# Certificate Common Names are MQTT usernames because use_identity_as_username
# is enabled. Add a distinct certificate and the narrowest possible entries for
# every real client; never share private keys between hosts or services.

user mqtt-health
topic write edsys/test/v1/health/mqtt-health/#

# Dedicated broker/restore audit identity. It cannot publish, acknowledge, or
# read HA/Frigate state; its only capability is detecting a stale HA command.
user command-audit
topic read edsys/v1/command/ha/#

# External Node-RED connection is intentionally read/derived-state only. Its
# separate internal 8884 connection submits non-retained automation requests.
user nodered
topic read edsys/v1/telemetry/#
topic read edsys/v1/state/#
topic read edsys/v1/availability/#
topic read edsys/v1/automation/ack/#
topic read edsys/test/v1/replay/#
topic write edsys/v1/state/derived/#
topic write edsys/v1/availability/edcore-automation/nodered/#

user telegraf
topic read edsys/v1/telemetry/environment/#
topic read edsys/v1/telemetry/energy/#
topic read edsys/v1/telemetry/rf/#
topic read edsys/v1/telemetry/highrate/#

user event-replay
topic read edsys/v1/telemetry/#
topic read edsys/v1/state/#
topic read edsys/v1/availability/#
topic write edsys/test/v1/replay/#
topic write edsys/v1/availability/edcore-automation/event-replay

# Migration identities. Issue distinct certificates only when each client is
# ready; never reuse the Home Assistant or Frigate private key.
user homeassistant
topic readwrite homeassistant/#
topic read frigate/#
topic read edsys/v1/telemetry/#
topic read edsys/v1/state/#
topic read edsys/v1/availability/#
topic write edsys/v1/telemetry/homeassistant/#
topic write edsys/v1/state/homeassistant/#
topic write edsys/v1/availability/homeassistant/#
topic read edsys/v1/command/ha/#
topic write edsys/v1/automation/ack/homeassistant/#

user frigate
topic readwrite frigate/#
topic read homeassistant/status
topic write homeassistant/#
topic write edsys/v1/telemetry/frigate/#
topic write edsys/v1/availability/frigate/#

# Issued only for a bounded synthetic ingestion/replay acceptance, then marked
# unused-not-delivered and removed online. It has no command/control access.
user edsys-edge-livingroom
topic write edsys/v1/telemetry/environment/edge-livingroom/#
topic write edsys/v1/state/edge-livingroom/#
topic write edsys/v1/availability/edge-livingroom/#
